Not entirely. "Has been dead" is one of those syntactically bizarre phrases=
 that Lojban is designed to avoid. It's not implicit, but the syntax leans =
towards "was at one time dead, but is no longer dead". "Was and is still de=
ad" is, rather more simply, "dead".

